The seed feeds listed in deploy/crowd/sources.json and
deploy/crowd/harvest-sources.json point at third-party public v2ray config
collections (v2rayNG-style subscription lists). Those lists are the works of
their respective authors, are used here as generic public feeds, and carry no
affiliation or endorsement on either side. Each repository is governed by its
own license and terms.

deploy/crowd/telegram-channels.json lists public Telegram channels that post
free proxy configurations. Simorgh reads their public pages the same way a
browser would; it does not host, verify, or endorse those channels.

No server in this repository is operated by the Simorgh project. The project
signs the published lists (see README.md) so apps can tell a genuine list from
a substitute served by a CDN or a filtering network; the signing key is a
repository secret and never lands in this repository.
